  "description": "SlideRule.Analyzers is the SlideRule build analyzer. It reports a broken architecture rule as a compiler warning at the offending code. The warning shows in the editor as you type and in plain 'dotnet build' output. It reads the rules from sliderule.model.json, which 'sliderule render --model' writes. It runs the same extractor and checker as 'sliderule check' over the project being compiled. 'sliderule check' stays the gate. The analyzer reports only the rules one project's compilation can decide, and never a violation 'check' would not. It needs a compiler on Roslyn 4.0.1 or later (the .NET 6 SDK, Visual Studio 2022). An older compiler builds as before, without the analyzer.",
  "developmentDependency": true,
